Tindra for Debian and Ubuntu
============================

Setup
-----

debconf asks for the public URL, the port, whether the reverse proxy is on
this machine, the database and the first account. With a local PostgreSQL
server it creates the role and database "tindra" itself. Change the answers
with:

  sudo dpkg-reconfigure tindra

When PostgreSQL is installed together with tindra (it's recommended), the
database is set up at the end of the installation, once PostgreSQL's own
setup is done; when it's installed later, as soon as it is. Until the public
URL and a database are configured, Tindra isn't started.

The configuration is /etc/tindra/tindra.env. dpkg-reconfigure manages
PUBLIC_URL, BIND_ADDR, TRUSTED_PROXIES, COOKIE_SECURE and DATABASE_URL;
add any other option (email, SSO, retention, limits) from
/usr/share/doc/tindra/examples/env.example, then:

  sudo systemctl restart tindra

(systemctl reload tindra applies changed project, event and user limits
without a restart.)

The CLI reads the same file when run as the tindra user, for example:

  sudo -u tindra tindra users create --email you@example.com --name "You"

Unattended installs
-------------------

Preseed the answers before installing, for example:

  tindra tindra/public_url string https://tindra.example.com
  tindra tindra/port string 8080
  tindra tindra/local_proxy boolean true
  tindra tindra/trusted_proxies string
  tindra tindra/local_database boolean true
  tindra tindra/database_url string
  tindra tindra/admin_email string you@example.com
  tindra tindra/admin_name string You
  tindra tindra/admin_password password <at least 12 characters>

  sudo debconf-set-selections answers.txt

The password is removed from debconf once the account exists.

Reverse proxy
-------------

Tindra serves plain HTTP; terminate TLS in front of it. Caddy:

  tindra.example.com {
      reverse_proxy localhost:8080
  }

nginx (with your certificate settings):

  server {
      listen 443 ssl;
      server_name tindra.example.com;

      location / {
          proxy_pass http://localhost:8080;
          proxy_set_header Host $host;
          proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
          proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
          proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
      }
  }

Backups
-------

Back up the database and /var/lib/tindra (source maps, attachments):

  sudo -u postgres pg_dump -Fc tindra > tindra.dump
  sudo tar -czf tindra-data.tar.gz -C /var/lib tindra

Purging the package removes /etc/tindra and /var/lib/tindra, not the
database. To drop it as well:

  sudo -u postgres dropdb tindra
  sudo -u postgres dropuser tindra
